  "title": "Breaking Change & Enhanced Testing for Integrations",
  "summary": "A breaking change has made the `eucHardeningDisposition` field read-only in `IntegrationVersion`. Additionally, new parameters and response fields are available for `TestIntegrationsRequest` and `TestIntegrationsResponse`, offering more control and insight into credential flows and EUC hardening during integration testing.",
  "details": "The `eucHardeningDisposition` property within the `GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaIntegrationVersion` schema is now `readOnly`. If your code previously attempted to set this field, it will now fail and requires an update. This field, which indicates the EUC hardening status, is now output-only and set by the service.\n\nFor integration testing, the `GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaTestIntegrationsRequest` now includes an optional `credentialMode` parameter. This allows you to specify the credential flow (e.g., `CREDENTIAL_MODE_HARDENED`) for synchronous tests, providing more control over how your integrations behave under different security contexts. The `GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaTestIntegrationsResponse` has been extended to include `credentialMode`, `eucHardeningDisposition`, and `hardenedPaths`. These new fields provide detailed insights into the credential flow used during the test, the integration's EUC hardening status, and which specific credential paths (like `SCRIPT_EVAL` or `SUB_INTEGRATION`) are covered by the hardened flow.\n\nFinally, the `GoogleInternalCloudCrmEventbusV3PostToQueueWithTriggerIdRequest` gains a `workflowId` field, enabling you to target and test specific integration versions, including unpublished drafts, by pinning the enqueue to that exact version.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
